 "verdict_reason": "No separate attacker exists. The 'attack' txs the MintSwap team cites (0xd2337efb, 0x29edec50) are Yoink's own, landing at index 0 of blocks 19563164/19563165. Etherscan's complete transfer history of the pool shows no vMINT sold into it before Yoink's tx (the sell path was never called by anyone, pre-exploit the pool saw the LP deposit, 8 successful buys (6 users, 2 small arb buys) and 2 reverted user buys), and no other actor sold into it until after Yoink: 2 small sells by another searcher in blocks 19563191/19563193 (late copy, 0.78 ETH). The only third-party tx Yoink beat is an innocent user's still-pending 5,991 vMINT sell (public mempool, first seen 19:49:25.637, 9.4 s before the block), which reverted afterwards; Yoink's tx is a different construction (314x the amount, min-out 1 wei, own recipient), so it is not a replay, and whether that sighting triggered the bot is unproven (its follow-up sells had no trigger). Yoink's txs are private (absent from mempool-dumpster); Unknown != none for a private attacker tx, but none was found on chain.",
